#!/usr/bin/env qore
# -*- mode: qore; indent-tabs-mode: nil -*-
# test-platform: macos - HTTP/1.x interim and 101 responses read from TCP and TLS sockets and the close of the connection
# Copyright (C) 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

# Every HTTP/1.x 1xx response other than 101 is an interim response (RFC 9110 section 15.2): the client skips it,
# whatever its code (100, 102, 103 or one not defined yet), and returns the final response that follows it on the
# same connection, which alone decides whether the connection is reused; the header of a 103 response is reported to
# an event queue.  More interim responses than the client accepts fail the request, and a 101 response to a request
# that did not ask for a protocol upgrade fails it at once, whether the response is streamed or not, and closes the
# connection (qore#7483).  Both the HTTPClient class and the HttpClientIo connection manager are tested.

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../../qlib"
%requires QUnit
%requires HttpClientIo

%exec-class HttpClientInterimResponsesTest

#! a self-signed certificate for localhost, for the TLS server
